NickelOS: Android follows ChromeOS's time zone (Waydroid gives Android
none, so it showed UTC). The zone is in Android's properties at each
start, for a new Android, and set through Android's AlarmManager once
Android has booted and whenever ChromeOS's zone changes, since Android
keeps the zone it saved itself. /etc/localtime links through
/var/lib/timezone/localtime to /usr/share/zoneinfo/<zone>.

